    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: an owner response must carry `bulkSignupWarning: true` once **more than 80** owners have already been created on today's business day, else `false`.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field/getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnersCreatedToday.java`** (new) \u2014 extracted the \"count owners registered on today's business day\" logic that was previously inline in `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`. This is now the single home for that count, reused by both the per-day limit and the new warning. It relies on the existing `BusinessDay` weekend roll-forward, keeping both rules bucketing by the same adjusted day.\n\n3. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit.java`** \u2014 refactored to call `OwnersCreatedToday.count(...)` instead of duplicating the loop, so its responsibility is just the limit decision.\n\n4. **`BulkSignupWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 the single definition of the warning threshold (`> 80`) and decision, delegating the count to `OwnersCreatedToday`.\n\n5. **Responders** (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`) \u2014 each now sets `dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignupWarning.isRaised(ownerRepository))` when building the response DTO, so every full owner response (GET/POST/PUT) carries an accurate, response-time value.\n\n### Design notes\n- The warning depends on live repository state, not on a single owner, so it belongs at response-construction time (the responders) rather than in the pure `OwnerMapper`, which stays a per-owner transform.\n- Counting logic lives in one small class reused by both the limit and warning rules \u2014 no copy-paste, each class keeps a single responsibility.\n\nThe acceptance test (`GET` after a fresh create asserts `bulkSignupWarning == false`) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
